'''{{D|Void}} Damage''' is a special damage type that is almost exclusive to [[Operator]]s, their [[Amp]]s, and {{WF|Xaku}}. Deals increased damage to {{D|Overguard}} and {{D|Zariman}} Void manifestations, but is otherwise neutral to all other health types meaning its damage is neither increased or decreased against most targets. Its [[Status Effect]] creates a field on the target that attracts bullets.

{{D|Void}} damage also provides unique advantages and uses, most notably against {{Faction|Sentient}} enemies (with the exception of Xaku's abilities):

*Guarantees a stun against drone-type Sentients like [[Battalyst]]s and [[Conculyst]]s.
*Nullifies any damage resistance developed by drone-type Sentients and the [[Shadow Stalker]].
*Bypasses certain invulnerabilities possessed by [[Eidolon]]-type Sentient like the [[Eidolon Vomvalyst]], [[Eidolon Teralyst]], and the [[Ropalolyst]].
*Destroy [[Kuva]] clouds in [[Kuva Siphon]] missions.
*Force [[Profit-Taker Orb]]'s shields to adopt another damage type weakness.
*Opens the [[Corpus Gas City#Secret Laboratories|Secret Laboratory]] doors in the [[Corpus Gas City]].
*Activate a [[Cambion Drift#Requiem Obelisk|Requiem Obelisk]] in the [[Cambion Drift]].
*Properly open an [[Isolation Vault]] in the Cambion Drift.
**Restore [[Loid]] and [[Otak]]'s health.
*Seal Void Rifts in [[Void Cascade]].
*Kill the [[Thrax Centurion]]'s and [[Thrax Legatus]]' spectral forms.
*Kill the [[Void Angel]]'s Ethereal form.

==[[Status Effect]]s==
The Status Effect of {{D|Void}} damage is '''Bullet Attractor''', which creates a small '''2.5''' meter radius field centered on where the target was shot for '''3''' seconds (e.g. proccing {{D|Void}} on the target's head creates the Bullet Attractor field centered on their head, proccing on their feet centers the field on their feet). Hit-scan bullets and projectiles that are shot into the field will be redirected towards the target.

If the projectile has [[Punch Through]], the projectile will "orbit" in the field after hitting the main target, making them unlikely to hit the main target more than once. As such, the attractor is not as synergistic with Punch Through as the similar {{A|Magnetize}}, though tightly packed enemies can be damaged by the orbiting projectiles. If the status effect expires while projectiles are still in the field, they will shoot out in effectively random directions and might hit more enemies.

Afflicted enemies will also have their own projectiles redirected, preventing them from properly shooting the player.

==Void Sources==
*{{D|Void}} damage can be found in the [[Operator]]'s Void powers, which include:
**[[Void Beam]]/[[Amp]] (Operator attack)
**[[Void Sling]]
*{{D|Void}} damage is part of Warframe {{WF|Xaku}}'s Abilities:
**{{A|Xata's Whisper}} ([[Helminth]] subsumable)
**{{A|Grasp of Lohk}}
**{{A|The Lost}} (Deny sub-ability)
**{{A|The Vast Untime}}
*{{M|Astral Bond}} allows [[Companion]]s to deal {{D|Void}} damage.
*{{Resource|Nonono}}

{{DamageTypeTable|Void}}

==Notes==
*{{D|Void}} damage is neither physical nor elemental; as such it receives no increases from {{Focus|Madurai}}'s {{Focus|Phoenix Talons}} and conversely it receives no penalties against resistances generated from [[Sortie]] conditions (Physical or Elemental Enhancements).
*{{WF|Xaku}}'s {{D|Void}} damage is only capable of proccing its Bullet Attractor status and resetting Sentient resistances, and only {{A|Xata's Whisper}} and {{A|The Lost}}'s Deny can do this. It lacks all other benefits, including bypassing [[Eidolon]]-type Sentient invulnerabilities and changing [[Profit-Taker Orb]]'s shield weakness. However, all its abilities still deal bonus damage to {{D|Overguard}} and {{D|Zariman}}.

